      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(mcp-apps): support bounded model context updates",
        "body": "Related: #111124\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nMCP Apps could not provide bounded, ephemeral context for the next user turn even though `@modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps` 1.7.4 defines `ui/update-model-context`. OpenClaw exposed no host capability, Gateway method, session ownership, or next-turn injection path for that request.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds the complete bounded path: advertise text updates only for live interactive views, validate exactly one text block up to 16 KiB, retain only the latest in-memory snapshot per session/view, and lease it to the next normal user turn exactly once. Pre-start failures roll the lease back; reset, expiry, read-only, unauthorized, and reconstructed-view paths reject or clear it. The original transcript prompt remains byte-for-byte unchanged, and no persistence or background turn is introduced.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; the author reviewed the full behavior and final diff.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInteractive MCP Apps can update the model's context for the next confirmed `ui/message` or other normal user turn. Updates never start a turn themselves, newer updates replace older ones, and unsupported or oversized payloads fail closed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Directly audited the tagged and published `@modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps` 1.7.4 source, types, docs, and AppBridge behavior.\n- Blacksmith Testbox focused matrix: helper validation/reservation, Gateway auth and bounds, agent exactly-once/transcript behavior, session cleanup/reset, resource expiry, and UI capability/handler tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `pnpm check:changed` passed across core, core tests, and UI lanes; `pnpm build` passed including the packaged Gateway and Control UI surfaces.\n- Real Chromium conformance flow passed: the official ext-apps app sent a model-context update, the confirmed `ui/message` observed it, and the standalone read-only host did not advertise the capability.\n- Final post-fix autoreview: no findings.\n",
        "branch": "codex/mcp-app-update-model-context",
